    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="19.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 19.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="19.1" corresp="#wit-g-a">⁊ word ⁊ weorc freonda gehwylc fadige mid rihte, ⁊ að ⁊ wedd wærlice healde.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="19.1" corresp="#wit-a">And word ⁊ weorc freonda gehwylc fadige mid rihte, ⁊ að ⁊ wead wearlice healde.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="19.1" corresp="#wit-b">⁊ word a[nd] weorc freonda gehwylc fadige mid rihte, ⁊ að ⁊ wed wærlice healde.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="19.1" corresp="#wit-q">Et quisquis amicus Dei est, uerbis et operibus rectitudinem flagitet, fidem et sacramenta caute custodiat.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="19.1" corresp="#wit-b">⁊ word ⁊ weorc freonda gehwylc fadige mid rihte ⁊ að ⁊ wed wærlice healde.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And word and weorc freonda gehwylc fadige mid rihte, and að and wedd wærlice healde.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und ordne der Freunde jeglicher Wort und Werk gerecht und halte sorgsam Eid und Versprechen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let each of [our] friends order word and work rightly and carefully keep oath and pledge.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">And everyone of our friends shall order his words and deeds aright, and strictly abide by his oath and pledge.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And all of our friends must order their words and deeds properly, and carefully uphold their oath and pledge.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="301"><ref target="clause:VIAtr_28">VI Atr 28</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 28</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="357"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:Af_1">Af 1</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 19:1-2: Cn 1018 18-19  VI Atr 28-28:1  Af 1</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="357"><label>quoted verbatim (bold in Wormald's table)</label> <ref target="clause:VIAtr_28">VI Atr 28–28.1</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 19:1-2: Cn 1018 18-19  VI Atr 28-28:1  Af 1</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="357"><label>quoted verbatim (bold in Wormald's table)</label> <ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-053">Cn 1018 18–19</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 19:1-2: Cn 1018 18-19  VI Atr 28-28:1  Af 1</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#kennedy" n="59"><ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-051">Cn 1018 17–18</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares VI Atr 28.; Robertson (p. 139) takes I Cn from B, which begins at ‘mæssedæg’ in 14.2, the earlier clauses being supplied from G</note>
      </div>
